(a) be bound and any ring binder folder must be in fully working order;

(b) be paginated (page numbering must not reduce the font size of any
document below 12 points);

(c) contain an index at the front referring to relevant page numbers;

(d) be in chronological order (except core bundles which must follow the
relevant core bundle index);

(e) not include original material such as photographs or recorded media;

(f) be on single-sided paper;

(g) be labelled on the front with the case title, case reference number and
type of bundle e.g. Permission to Appeal Bundle.
